From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:20:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] repeater: pick the smallest adequate buffer (1.05x
 segment cap, was 1.5x)

Repeaters should be as small as the wire segment allows; the 1.5x margin
oversized them. OpenROAD's post-hoc resizer already defaults to large
buffers (the measured ibex P&R-growth cause), so the synthesis-side
pre-buffering should lean small.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
---
 src/map/scl/sclDrc.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/map/scl/sclDrc.c b/src/map/scl/sclDrc.c
index c231d7561..c621302ae 100644
--- a/src/map/scl/sclDrc.c
+++ b/src/map/scl/sclDrc.c
@@ -223,7 +223,11 @@ int Abc_SclInsertRepeaters( SC_Lib * pLib, Abc_Ntk_t * pNtk, float LcritUm,
         SC_RingForEachCell( pBufClass->pRepr, pTemp, t )
         {
             SC_Pin * pPo = SC_CellPin( pTemp, pTemp->n_inputs );
-            if ( pPo->max_out_cap >= 1.5 * SegCap )
+            // smallest buffer whose drive covers one Lcrit segment (a small
+            // margin, not 1.5x): repeaters should be as small as the wire
+            // allows -- OpenROAD's post-hoc resizer otherwise defaults to
+            // large buffers, the measured P&R-growth cause on ibex.
+            if ( pPo->max_out_cap >= 1.05 * SegCap )
             {
                 pBufCell = pTemp;
                 break;
-- 
